menu "C6 LINK (SPI slave to TC275, myCar doc 22)"

    config C6_LINK_SPI_SCLK_GPIO
        int "LINK SPI SCLK GPIO (from TC275 P33.11)"
        default 19
        help
            Wiring is the single source of truth: myCar 23-wiring.md §9.1
            (X1-3 P33.11 SCLK -> J3-9 GPIO19).

    config C6_LINK_SPI_MOSI_GPIO
        int "LINK SPI MOSI GPIO (from TC275 P33.12)"
        default 18
        help
            23-wiring.md §9.1: X1-4 P33.12 MTSR -> J3-10 GPIO18.

    config C6_LINK_SPI_MISO_GPIO
        int "LINK SPI MISO GPIO (to TC275 P33.13)"
        default 20
        help
            23-wiring.md §9.1: X1-5 P33.13 MRST <- J3-8 GPIO20.

    config C6_LINK_SPI_CS_GPIO
        int "LINK SPI CS GPIO (from TC275 P23.4 SLSO5)"
        default 23
        help
            23-wiring.md §9.1: X1-12 P23.4 SLSO5 -> J3-5 GPIO23.

    config C6_LINK_SPI_IRQ_GPIO
        int "LINK data-ready IRQ GPIO (open-drain, to TC275 P23.0)"
        default 21
        help
            23-wiring.md §9.1: J3-7 GPIO21 -> X1-8 P23.0 (IOM edge IRQ).
            Open-drain; the 10k pull-up to 3V3 is external hardware
            (22 §3.2 - without it the link degrades to pure polling).

    config C6_LINK_SPI_CLOCK_HZ
        int "Production clock step (master-driven, diag mirror)"
        default 5000000
        range 1000000 20000000
        help
            The master owns the clock; this value is what the slave reports
            in diagnostics and what the TC275 side should be configured to.
            Ladder per 22 §8 G5: 1/2/5/10/20 MHz, production baseline 5 MHz.

    config C6_LINK_DEBUG_UART_RX_GPIO
        int "Debug console RX GPIO (documentation anchor)"
        default 6
        help
            23-wiring.md §2: GPIO6/7 are the debug console (J1-5/6) - the
            UART is NOT used by the LINK anymore (T3: former TX=10/RX=11
            defaults were wrong and are deleted).  Kept here so that
            documentation, Kconfig and hardware agree.

    config C6_LINK_DEBUG_UART_TX_GPIO
        int "Debug console TX GPIO (documentation anchor)"
        default 7

endmenu
